Source-landscape note: The 2023 U.S. welfare documentary universe is broad and institutionally diverse, spanning federal rules and performance reports, GAO audits, CMS/HHS administrative records, HUD homelessness data, KFF and Urban Institute analyses, civil-rights enforcement, congressional materials, academic research, and national/local journalism. Major discovery families include health coverage and Medicaid unwinding, housing and homelessness, food insecurity, child care and education, disability and equal opportunity, administrative capacity, oversight, and longer-term life chances. Results include favorable, adverse, and mixed perspectives; several congressional records and PDFs may require later access verification.

